<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7018" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cāsŭālis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		casus. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Casual</i>, <i>fortuitous</i>
			(post-class. and very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">condicio,</span>”
				<i>depending upon chance</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 6, 51, 1, § 7</span></i>
			.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cāsŭālĭter</span></b> , <i>accidentally</i>, <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep.
				9, 11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Fulg. Myth. 1,
			5</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			gram., <i>relating to</i> or <i>declined
				with cases</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Casuale, ut ab equo: equum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 8, § 52, p.
				116</span></i>
			 Bip.; cf. <i><span class="en">id. ib. 10</span></i>, § 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">18, p. 164 Bip.: formae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prisc. p. 672</span></i>
			 P. al.</div>
